cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Nabd software, hardware designs, or data, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
title: "Nabd: an open network of GPS-synchronized ESP32 nodes for grid frequency and synchrophasor measurement"
abstract: >-
  Nabd is an open network of low-cost GPS-synchronized ESP32-S3 nodes that
  measure power grid frequency, rate of change of frequency (ROCOF), and voltage
  synchrophasors following the P class of IEEE C37.118.1. The project contains
  the node firmware, a collector that stores time-aligned measurements as
  Parquet files, event detection, a live map, a compliance test harness, KiCad
  hardware designs, and an open dataset.
authors:
